title: 'pallet-xcm: make `claim_assets` weight scale with the number of claimed assets'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `claim_assets` was previously charged a flat weight benchmarked with a single
    asset, while a claim may contain up to `MAX_ITEMS_IN_ASSETS` (20) assets, each
    performing per-asset storage reads and writes through the `AssetTransactor`.
    The extrinsic is now annotated with a weight linear in the number of claimed
    assets and its benchmark is parameterized accordingly.

    Breaking change: `pallet_xcm::WeightInfo::claim_assets` now takes the number of
    assets as `n: u32`; chains with custom `pallet_xcm` weights must regenerate
    them. Chains whose `AssetTransactor` can deposit multiple distinct asset kinds
    (e.g. Asset Hub) must override the new (defaulted)
    `pallet_xcm::benchmarking::Config::get_assets` method so the benchmark measures
    a real per-asset weight slope; the default merges into a single asset entry and
    measures a flat weight, which is only sound for single-asset-kind transactors
    (e.g. relay chains). `VersionedAssets` gained `len()` and `is_empty()`.
